# Optional CUDA build of PyTorch, for instructors or students with an NVIDIA GPU.
#
# No lab requires a GPU — weeks 3 to 6 are sized to finish on a laptop CPU inside the
# lab slot. This file exists only to make an available GPU usable, never to make one
# necessary. The one place a GPU genuinely helps is the W4D3 detection fine-tune
# stretch section, which is why that section also ships a Colab path.
#
# Install the base stack first, then override torch:
#
#   uv pip install -r requirements.lock
#   uv pip install -r requirements-gpu.in
#
# Check your CUDA version with `nvidia-smi` and swap cu121 for the matching build.
# Apple silicon needs nothing here — the default wheels use MPS, and aiep.env.device()
# picks it up automatically.

--index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

